# Greptile review gate

- Never push code immediately after committing.
- Every commit must complete `npm run review:greptile`; Greptile reviews
  committed branch changes and ignores the working tree.
- Read `.git/greptile/latest.txt`. Fix every valid P0/P1 finding and every P2
  that indicates correctness, security, performance, or maintainability risk.
- Do not apply feedback blindly. Verify the claim against code/docs, fix the
  root cause, add a regression test, and rerun the relevant Pappal verification.
- Commit the fix; the post-commit hook starts a fresh review for the new HEAD.
- Before any push, run `npm run review:greptile:status`. Do not bypass the
  pre-push hook or push while review is absent, running, failed, or has findings.
- Pull/merge requests must keep Greptile update reviews enabled. Address new
  findings before merge; the Greptile status check is required, not advisory.
- A completed AI review is one layer, not proof. Typecheck, lint, tests,
  security scans, database checks, Android build checks, and device evidence
  remain authoritative for their domains.
